# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment template for ddd-harness-engineering.
#
#   cp .env.example .env          (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# Then fill in MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_KEY below. Everything else already has a
# working default and only needs to be set if you are overriding it.
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way -- it holds a live API key.
# Never commit it, never paste it into chat, never screen-share it.
#
# These variables are read by the `Settings` class in
# ddd_harness_engineering/__init__.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------------

# API key for the Microsoft Foundry (Azure AI Foundry) project.
#
# Where to get it:
#   Azure AI Foundry portal (https://ai.azure.com) -> select the project named
#   in MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT below -> Overview / "Keys and Endpoint" ->
#   copy Key 1 (or Key 2).
#   The Azure CLI equivalent:
#     az cognitiveservices account keys list -n <account> -g <resource-group>
#
# For the workshop the organisers distribute this key -- ask them rather than
# provisioning your own. Leave it blank here; fill it in only in your .env.
MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_KEY=


# --- Optional (defaults live in the Settings class; uncomment to override) ---
#
# Keep these commented out unless you are actually changing them. An empty
# value is NOT the same as an unset one -- `MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=` with
# nothing after it fails URL validation at startup, whereas omitting the line
# entirely gives you the default below.

# Foundry project endpoint. Must be a valid URL. The OpenAI-compatible base URL
# used by the client is derived from this (scheme + host + /openai/v1).
# Default:
# MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=https://datacation-deep-dive.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/proj-default

# Name of the model deployment to call -- this is the *deployment* name from the
# Foundry portal, which need not match the underlying model name.
# Default:
# MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-5.6-luna

# API version passed to the Foundry endpoint.
# Default:
# MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_API_VERSION=preview
